WEBVTT

NOTE Fictional focus group (Trama example project). Excerpt, first part only.

1
00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:17.225
<v Moderator>Thanks, everyone, for coming. To start, could you each say in a sentence what the garden means to you?</v>

2
00:00:17.825 --> 00:00:24.575
<v Linda>For me it’s my sanity. [laughter] No, really. I work in a call centre. Here nobody’s on hold.</v>

3
00:00:25.394 --> 00:00:34.019
<v Jamal>Community, I’d say. I’ve lived on the same street for six years and I knew nobody. Here I know forty people by name.</v>

4
00:00:35.057 --> 00:00:41.807
<v Rosa>Food. I’m serious. With three kids and the prices now, the plot is part of how we eat.</v>

5
00:00:43.064 --> 00:00:47.564
<v Peter>Peace and quiet. And the birds. I’ve counted twenty-six species since January.</v>

6
00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:53.165
<v Moderator>Jamal, you said you knew nobody before. How did that change?</v>

7
00:00:54.860 --> 00:01:10.235
<v Jamal>Slowly. The first months I just did my plot and left. Then Rosa’s kids started coming over to look at my chillies, and then Rosa came over to tell them off, and then we were talking. [laughter] Kids break the ice.</v>

8
00:01:11.049 --> 00:01:13.674
<v Rosa>They’re very good at breaking things. [laughter]</v>

9
00:01:14.707 --> 00:01:25.207
<v Linda>It took me a year to feel I belonged. The old hands have their own language. They say things like “second earlies” and “chitting” and you just nod.</v>

10
00:01:26.459 --> 00:01:27.209
<v Peter>Guilty. [laughter]</v>

11
00:01:28.680 --> 00:01:32.055
<v Moderator>Rosa, can you say more about the food side?</v>

12
00:01:33.745 --> 00:01:49.120
<v Rosa>Well, from June to October I hardly buy vegetables. I freeze beans, I make sauce with the tomatoes, my mother-in-law makes jam with whatever’s left. It’s not a hobby for us. If the plot went, we’d notice it at the till.</v>

13
00:01:49.929 --> 00:01:56.304
<v Linda>That’s the thing people don’t see. They think it’s all middle-class people growing kale for their photos.</v>

14
00:01:57.332 --> 00:01:59.207
<v Peter>Some of it is. [laughter]</v>

15
00:02:00.454 --> 00:02:02.704
<v Linda>Some of it is, fair enough.</v>

16
00:02:04.170 --> 00:02:08.670
<v Moderator>What about the relationships between plot holders? How do people get on?</v>
